[0.101, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mIf you hit a compiler bug, minim\u001b[36Gz\u001b[38G it first: bis\u001b[53Gct to the smallest source that still\u001b[90Gtriggers it, \u001b[104Gnd f\u001b[109Gnd the\u001b[116G\u001b[39m    \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mclos\u001b[8Gst vari\u001b[16Gnt that *does* compile, so the trigge\u001b[54G is\u001b[58Gp\u001b[60Gnned\u001b[65Gdown pr\u001b[73Gcise\u001b[78Gy (not\u001b[85Gjust \"my\u001b[94Gbig program failed\").\u001b[116GThen\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bwri\u001b[7Ge it to a\u001b[17G`BUG-<slug>.md` fi\u001b[36Ge in\u001b[41Gthe project root with\u001b[63Ga one-line title, the\u001b[85G`promise version` output, your \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bplatform, th\u001b[16G minimal repro (sm\u001b[35Gllest `.pr` s\u001b[49Gurce plus the exact `promise build`\u001b[85Gc\u001b[87Gmmand),\u001b[95Gth\u001b[98G verba\u001b[105Gim\u001b[108Gerror \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255moutput, the expected behavior,\u001b[34Ga short tabl\u001b[47G o\u001b[50G what\u001b[56Gdoes and doesn't trigger\u001b[81Git,\u001b[85Gyour best\u001b[95Gguess\u001b[101Gat \u001b[105Ghe cause, and\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Bthe workaround\u001b[18Gyou used in the real code. Verify\u001b[52Gthe \u001b[57Gepro actually fails and the \"compiles fine\" controls actually \r\u001b["]
[0.000, "o", "2C\u001b[1Bcompile before writing them down — don't go from memory.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m                                                                                                                \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mIf the task needs something Promi\u001b[37Ge doesn't have\u001b[52Gyet\u001b[56G— a standard-library module that\u001b[90Gsn'\u001b[94G there, or a missing \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mlangu\u001b[9Gge feature — don't fake i\u001b[35G silently. Build the closest clean th\u001b[74Gg you can, or, if it's a hard\u001b[104Gblocker, stop \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Band say why. Either way record\u001b[34Gthe\u001b[38Ggap in\u001b[46G `FEATURE-<slug>.md` file in the project root: a one-line title, the \u001b[39m     \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m`promise version` output, what\u001b[34Gyou n\u001b[40Geded\u001b[45Gand why\u001b[53Gthe\u001b[57Gtask called\u001b[69Gfor it, what's missing (e.g. no st\u001b[104Gndar\u001b[110Gm\u001b[112Gdule for\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BX, no\u001b[9Glanguage support for Y), whether it blocked you ou\u001b[60Gright or just forced a workaround, the workaround you used,\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Band — if you can — a **sketch of th"]
[0.000, "o", "e API or syntax** that would have made it clean.\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[39m                                                                                                                   \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mPut `Please file this upstream at https://g\u001b[47Gthub.\u001b[53Gom/promise-language/promis\u001b[80G/issues` at the \u001b[97Gop of any such file, \u001b[39m  \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mwrite one file per distinct\u001b[31Gissue, and mention each in your summary so I remember to submit it. Only write these for \r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mreal failures and real gaps — don't invent them.\u001b[39m                                                                      \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI'll\u001b[8Gstart\u001b[14Gby\u001b[17Glearning\u001b[26Gthe\u001b[30Glanguage\u001b[39Gfrom\u001b[44Gthe\u001b[48Gtoolchain.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1C\u001b[1B Reading \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m files, running \u001b[1m8\u001b[22m shell commands…\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ promise init --help; echo ===; promise build --help\r\u001b[2C\u001b[2B\u001b[38;2;215;119;87mBre\u001b[39m\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
