[0.017, "o", "\u001b[?25l\u001b[H\u001b[3G\u001b[48;2;55;55;55m\u001b[38;2;255;255;255mIf the task needs something Pr\u001b[34Gmise doesn't\u001b[47Ghave yet\u001b[56G— \u001b[59G standard-libr\u001b[74Gry\u001b[77Gmodu\u001b[83G that isn't there, or a missing \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Blanguage feature — don't fake it silently. Build the closest clean thing you can, or, if it's a hard blocker, stop \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1Band\u001b[7Gsay why. Either way record\u001b[34Gthe ga\u001b[41G in a `FEATURE-<slug>.md` file in the project roo\u001b[91G: a one-line title, the \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[2C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m`promise version` output, what you\u001b[38Gneeded and why the task called for it, what's missing (e.g. no standard\u001b[110Gmodule for\r\u001b[2C\u001b[1BX, no language support\u001b[26Gfor Y), whe\u001b[38Gher it blocked you outright or just forced a workaround, the workaround you used,\r\u001b[1B\u001b[39m  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mand — if you can — a **sketch of the API or syntax** that would have made it clean.\u001b[39m                                   \r\u001b[1B                                                                                                                   "]
[0.000, "o", "     \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mPut `Please file this upstream at https://github.com/promise-language/promise/issues` at the top of any such file, \u001b[39m   \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mwrite one file per distinct issue, and mention each in your summary so I remember to submit it. Only write these for \u001b[39m \r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;255;255;255mreal failures and real gaps — don't invent them.\u001b[39m                                                                      \r\u001b[1B\u001b[49m\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[3G\u001b[39mI'll\u001b[8Gstart\u001b[14Gby\u001b[17Glearning\u001b[26Gthe\u001b[30Glanguage\u001b[39Gfrom\u001b[44Gthe\u001b[48Gtoolchain.\r\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B  \u001b[38;2;153;153;153mRead\u001b[8G\u001b[1m2\u001b[22m files, ran \u001b[1m15\u001b[22m shell commands \u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;255;255;255m⏺\u001b[3G\u001b[39mNow let me\u001b[14Gverify\u001b[21Gthe\u001b[25Gtrickier\u001b[34Glanguage\u001b[43Gconstructs\u001b[54GI'll\u001b[59Gneed\u001b[64Gbefore\u001b[71Gwriting\u001b[79Gthe\u001b[83Greal\u001b[88Gthing.\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m⏺\u001b[3G\u001b[39mRunning \u001b[1m2\u001b[22m shell commands…\u001b[K\r\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153m  ⎿  $ S=/private/tmp/claude-501/-Us"]
[0.000, "o", "ers-xxxxx-prog-zoo-mini-git-mini-git-claude/27a900f2-a43e-4b95-bd87-c7052de02092/scr\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Batchpad; cd $S/t1 && python3 - <<'EOF'\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1Bim\u001b[9Gort re\u001b[39m\u001b[K\r\u001b[5C\u001b[1B\u001b[38;2;153;153;153mp='main.pr'; s=open(p).read()\r\u001b[6C\u001b[1B=s.replace('return Self(root: root, objects: path.join(root, \"objects\"));','return Self(root: root.clone…\u001b[39m\u001b[30;1H\u001b[28;3H\u001b[?25h"]
